import Poincare.L4.PointedGH.Transport
import Poincare.D12.GeometricCompactness.Criterion
import Poincare.D12.GeometricCompactness.Frontier

/-!
# Poincare.L4.PointedGH.Family
...
-/

open scoped Topology ENNReal Cardinal
open Set Filter Metric
open GromovHausdorff

namespace Poincare.L4.PointedGH

/-- **Explicit compatible-coupling data for pointed Gromov–Hausdorff convergence.**

Pointed GH convergence of a sequence `(X n, x n)` to `(X∞, x∞)` is *not* implied by unpointed
convergence `ghDist (X n) X∞ → 0`: the basepoints have to be matched.  This structure carries
exactly the explicit data that makes the pointed statement true:

* a coupling space `Z n` and isometric embeddings `Φ n : X n → Z n`, `Ψ n : X∞ → Z n`;
* a rate `ε n > 0` with `ε n → 0`;
* the *unpointed* compatibility `hausdorffDist (range (Φ n)) (range (Ψ n)) < ε n`;
* the *pointed* compatibility `dist (Φ n (x n)) (Ψ n x∞) < ε n`.

This is data (a `Type`-valued structure with fields), not a `Prop` interface: every field is an
explicit witness, which is what makes the basepoint-convergence assembly below a proof rather
than an appeal to an unproved convergence relation. -/
structure PointedGHCoupling (X : ℕ → Type) [∀ n, MetricSpace (X n)] (x : ∀ n, X n)
    (X∞ : Type) [MetricSpace X∞] (x∞ : X∞) where
  /-- coupling space at stage `n` -/
  Z : ℕ → Type
  /-- metric structure on each coupling space -/
  [instZ : ∀ n, MetricSpace (Z n)]
  /-- isometric embedding of the approximating space -/
  Φ : ∀ n, X n → Z n
  /-- isometric embedding of the limit space -/
  Ψ : ∀ n, X∞ → Z n
  isometry_Φ : ∀ n, Isometry (Φ n)
  isometry_Ψ : ∀ n, Isometry (Ψ n)
  /-- convergence rate -/
  ε : ℕ → ℝ
  ε_pos : ∀ n, 0 < ε n
  ε_tendsto : Tendsto ε atTop (𝓝 0)
  /-- unpointed compatibility: the coupled images have Hausdorff distance `< ε n` -/
  hausdorff_lt : ∀ n, hausdorffDist (range (Φ n)) (range (Ψ n)) < ε n
  /-- pointed compatibility: the coupled basepoints are `< ε n` apart -/
  basepoint_lt : ∀ n, dist (Φ n (x n)) (Ψ n x∞) < ε n
```

Then:
```lean
attribute [instance] PointedGHCoupling.instZ
```

Then theorems. One issue: with `[∀ n, MetricSpace (X n)]` as a structure parameter, referencing `PointedGHCoupling X x X∞ x∞` requires the instance to be synthesized. In theorem statements I'll include the instance binders.

Now `ghDist_tendsto`:
```lean
theorem PointedGHCoupling.ghDist_tendsto {X : ℕ → Type} [∀ n, MetricSpace (X n)]
    [∀ n, CompactSpace (X n)] [∀ n, Nonempty (X n)] {x : ∀ n, X n}
    {X∞ : Type} [MetricSpace X∞] [CompactSpace X∞] [Nonempty X∞] {x∞ : X∞}
    (D : PointedGHCoupling X x X∞ x∞) :
    Tendsto (fun n => ghDist (X n) X∞) atTop (𝓝 0) := by
  refine squeeze_zero (fun n => ?_) (fun n => ?_) D.ε_tendsto
  · rw [ghDist]; exact dist_nonneg
  · calc
      ghDist (X n) X∞ ≤ hausdorffDist (range (D.Φ n)) (range (D.Ψ n)) :=
        ghDist_le_hausdorffDist (D.isometry_Φ n) (D.isometry_Ψ n)
      _ ≤ D.ε n := le_of_lt (D.hausdorff_lt n)
```
Note `ghDist (X n) X∞` — universe: X : ℕ → Type (Type 0), X∞ : Type. Good.

`ghDist_le_hausdorffDist` needs `{γ : Type w} [MetricSpace γ] {Φ : X → γ} {Ψ : Y → γ} (ha : Isometry Φ) (hb : Isometry Ψ)`. Since `D.Φ n : X n → D.Z n` — the type `D.Z n` has an instance from `D.instZ n`. The structure field `instZ` is an instance field, so within the structure it's fine; but in the theorem, will the instance `∀ n, MetricSpace (D.Z n)` be found? I declared `attribute [instance] PointedGHCoupling.instZ` globally, which registers the projection as an instance, and it takes `D` as an argument, so `MetricSpace (D.Z n)` is synthesizable via `PointedGHCoupling.instZ D n`. Good.

